SDL-E1018 (spec/README.md#design-rules-settled)

  x `fn::name()` is a call — the `function` clause takes a name path (remove `()`)
   ,----
 1 | analyzer a { function: fn::name(); };
   :                        ^^^^^|^^^^
   :                             `-- not a well-formed function path
   `----
  help: an analyzer function is a name path — `fn::name`, `fn::module::name`, or `mod::module[::name…]` — never a call
